# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT — TOWERTECH SOCIETY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

## Project Overview

Develop, improve, and integrate all requested features into the existing **TowerTech Residential Society Management System**, using the current application, database, authentication, role assignments, UI components, and design system.

The society name throughout the application must be:

**Joyville Sensorium**

The objective is to make TowerTech a functional, secure, professional, and fully integrated residential society management platform.

## CRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS

1. Work on the existing TowerTech application. Do not create a separate application or rebuild it from scratch.
2. Implement all requirements in Sections 1–14, including every requested module change and the complete Financial Management Module.
3. Preserve the existing theme, colors, typography, sidebar, navigation style, layout conventions, and responsive design. Do not redesign the application unnecessarily.
4. Inspect the existing codebase, database schema, authentication system, and current module implementations before making changes.
5. Reuse existing components, database tables, APIs, relationships, and authentication wherever appropriate.
6. Preserve all unrelated working functionality. Make targeted changes instead of replacing entire modules without need.
7. All forms, buttons, filters, approvals, calculations, charts, notifications, and reports must work. Do not create static mockups or fake functionality.
8. Use actual database records. Do not introduce hardcoded financial totals, fake residents, fake visitors, fake transactions, or fabricated payment confirmations.
9. Enforce role permissions in backend APIs and database security policies, not just by hiding buttons in the frontend.
10. Test every changed module and its interactions with the other modules before considering implementation complete.

